Thank you, that's a careful review. My answers, as the owner's driver:

1. Do not revise the design in this review. Keep the verdicts as you proposed them (`revised_design: false`). Record your four design questions as recommendations for the next design revision, not decided now:
   - the momentum prediction range of −30 to 30 m/s, where I agree the design is wrong and the build is right;
   - binding input-error wording with the symbol, the unit and the value entered;
   - letter-spacing tokens;
   - the scaled playback speed, each run shown in 1.5 to 12 s with the clock showing simulated time. I accept it as built for now.
2. The implementation deltas (items 1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12, 13) stand as deltas against this Alpha. Item 10, the momentum "Why" sentence contradicting the numbers, and item 8, the skip link that does nothing on two labs, are the ones I'd fix first.
3. Please correct `observed_on`. Nothing was rendered by you or by me: I read the served HTML, CSS and scripts over HTTP through the relay. Use the value the review schema allows that does not claim a browser rendering. If the schema has no such value, keep it and state plainly in the review that nothing was rendered. R7.1 and R8.20 stay "not observed" as you wrote them.

Then save the review as it stands.

I've saved the review as it stands in `.surety/design/reviews/review-1.json`. The verdicts are the same as I proposed (all three labs `deltas`) and `revised_design` is still false. I haven't changed the design.

**observed_on.** The review schema allows only browser, simulator, emulator, device and simulation. None of them means "read over HTTP, not rendered". "simulation" would say something else that is also false. So I kept `browser`, as you said. The schema has no free-text field for a whole screen, so every delta now ends with this: "Nothing was rendered: this rests on the served HTML, CSS and scripts read over HTTP. observed_on says "browser" only because the review schema has no value for a read that is not rendered." R7.1 and R8.20 stay "not observed". Human-judged criteria have no place in the review schema, so there's nothing in the file to change for them.

**Design recommendations.** Each design delta now begins "Recommendation for the next design revision, not decided in this review":
- the momentum prediction range of −30 to 30 m/s (you agree the design is wrong and the build is right);
- binding input-error wording with the symbol, the unit and the value entered (still `both`, because the build has to follow it);
- letter-spacing tokens;
- scaled playback, each run shown in 1.5 to 12 s with the clock showing simulated time. This one is new: a `design` delta on the `run` state of all three labs, noting that you accept it as built for now.

**Implementation deltas.** Items 1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12 and 13 are unchanged as deltas against this Alpha. The deltas for the momentum "Why" sentence (10) and the skip link on friction and trajectory (8) now say you'd fix them first.

The verdicts are still proposals for you to confirm. Once you have, I'd propose closing this session.
